{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Like the cold of snow</b> — cooling. And it is possible that it is from צנה וסוחרה, because just as it protects a person at harvest time from the heat, so a faithful messenger." "<b>And the soul</b> — defective. Its meaning: like the desire of his master's soul, he brings back answer to him; likewise: כי נפש הוא חובל — deficient חי." "Another interpretation: <b>and his master's soul</b> — as though the master's soul cleaved to the messenger as he goes and comes; he restores them to his inward part by his faithfulness."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:38.560027039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}